Link libatomic for mingw to satisfy clang's size-generic atomic libcalls.

Clang emits calls to the size-generic libcall __atomic_compare_exchange
for some v8 atomic ops (e.g. ExternalPointerTable, Factory::NewForeign,
ConcurrentMarking::RunMajor). On mingw/ucrt64:

  - libgcc.a does NOT export __atomic_compare_exchange (size-generic);
    it only exposes the size-specific __atomic_compare_exchange_<N>.
  - compiler-rt builtins are not installed.
  - libatomic.a exports both the size-generic and size-specific variants.

Chromium's link uses an explicit lib list (-nodefaultlibs style) and so
nothing pulls libatomic in transitively. Add 'atomic' to the mingw
default_libs so every link picks it up; --gc-sections drops it where
unused.

GCC's codegen on the same source tends to emit the size-specific call
which libgcc satisfies, so the GCC build was unaffected. Adding atomic
is benign for both compilers.

--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/build/config/BUILD.gn
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/build/config/BUILD.gn
@@ -230,6 +230,11 @@ config("default_libs") {
       "kernel32",
       "ole32",
     ]
+    if (!is_clang) {
+      libs += [
+        "atomic"
+      ]
+    }
   } else if (is_android) {
     libs = [
       "dl",
